@prefix lv2:    <http://lv2plug.in/ns/lv2core#> .
@prefix owl:    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ui:     <http://lv2plug.in/ns/extensions/ui#> .
@prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix zyngui: <http://zynthian.org/ns/lv2/zyngui#> .

<http://zynthian.org/ns/lv2/zyngui>
	a owl:Ontology ;
	rdfs:label "Zynthian UI widgets" ;
	rdfs:comment """
Zynthian widgets are Python/Tk modules that zynthian-ui loads to display a
plugin's custom GUI on the Zynthian screen. They are declared with the standard
LV2 UI mechanism (ui:ui), using zyngui:widget as the UI class. ui:binary points
to the Python module, named zynthian_widget_<name>.py, which must define a class
named zynthian_widget_<name> derived from zyngui.zynthian_widget_base.

The plugin's own bundle can declare a widget, or a separate extension bundle can
do it for an existing plugin. In that case the extension bundle must NOT declare
the plugin as lv2:Plugin; it adds only the ui:ui triple. A single bundle can
declare widgets for several plugins, and several plugins can share one widget.
""" .

zyngui:widget
	a rdfs:Class , owl:Class ;
	rdfs:subClassOf ui:UI ;
	rdfs:label "Zynthian widget" ;
	rdfs:comment "Python/Tk widget run inside zynthian-ui. ui:binary is the Python module." .

zyngui:apiVersion
	a rdf:Property , owl:DatatypeProperty ;
	rdfs:domain zyngui:widget ;
	rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
	rdfs:label "API version" ;
	rdfs:comment "Version of the zynthian_widget_base API the widget was written for." .

zyngui:help
	a rdf:Property , owl:ObjectProperty ;
	rdfs:domain zyngui:widget ;
	rdfs:label "help page" ;
	rdfs:comment """Optional HTML help page for the widget, shown by the zynthian help screen.
Write plain HTML (a full page or just a fragment): the zynthian-help stylesheet and
the "help_ui" body class are added automatically, so it looks like the other help
pages. Stylesheets linked by the page are applied after it and can override it.""" .
